        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(release): reconcile contribution provenance",
        "body": "Closes #103429\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where release maintainers could generate an incomplete contribution record because the verifier treated first-parent history as the source inventory and allowed contextual references to stand in for source-PR ownership.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe verifier now inventories the complete raw Git DAG from the unique merge base, rejects shallow/grafted/replaced history, and assigns each commit through auditable GitHub associations, strict merged-PR directives, exact cherry-pick/patch provenance, verified revert parity, or direct-commit classification. It also records canonical/current/generated/missing/stale sets and accepts only one association-free `CHANGELOG.md` tail after the immutable source cutoff.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRelease maintainers get a deterministic, fail-closed contribution manifest with complete source-PR credit, direct-commit auditability, explicit shipped/reverted exclusions, and concrete reconciliation metrics before publication.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kx5zaabyb1aag43tgncd5ytt`: 55/55 focused verifier, pagination, inventory, and ledger tests passed.\n- Targeted `oxfmt --check` passed for the changed verifier and test files.\n- Full-history preflight uses a non-shallow clone with no grafts or replacement refs; Git connectivity verification passes.\n- Historical `2026.7.1` reconciliation is running against the exact `7ebe237b67d3d57bd027b71d4ae415f90d4d8cab -> 811ddd96180583bae00001f71971419182ae0520` source/final target model.\n- Fresh structured autoreview and repo-native prepare/merge gates will be attached before landing.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n",
